{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JER",
  "chapter": 47,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JER.47.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.47.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The word of the LORD that came to Jeremiah the prophet against the Philistines, before Pharaoh smote Gaza.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.47.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.47.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD; Behold, waters rise out of the north, and shall be an overflowing flood, and shall overflow the land, and all that is in it; the city, and them that dwell therein: then the men shall cry, and all the inhabitants of the land shall howl.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.47.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.47.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At the noise of the stamping of the hoofs of his strong ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "horses",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", at the rushing of his chariots, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and at",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the rumbling of his wheels, the fathers shall not look back to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " children for feebleness of hands:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.47.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.47.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because of the day that cometh to lay waste all the Philistines, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to cut off from Tyre and Zidon every helper that remaineth: for the LORD will lay waste the Philistines, the remnant of the country of Caphtor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.47.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.47.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Baldness is come upon Gaza; Ashkelon is cut off ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the remnant of their valley: how long wilt thou cut thyself?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.47.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.47.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O thou sword of the LORD, how long ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will it be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ere thou be quiet? put up thyself into thy scabbard, rest, and be still.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.47.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.47.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How can it be quiet, seeing the LORD hath given it a charge against Ashkelon, and against the sea shore? there hath he appointed it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
